Third-party code
================

This product includes software adapted from Whoops
(https://github.com/kryoseu/whoops), by kryoseu and the Whoops contributors,
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0: see LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt.
Whoops' export import comes from its fork's CSV import
(https://github.com/vchatela-org/whoops, branch feat/csv-import), offered
upstream as https://github.com/kryoseu/whoops/pull/5.

The adapted files say so in their header ("Portions adapted from
kryoseu/whoops (https://github.com/kryoseu/whoops), Apache License 2.0;
modified."), and remain under the Apache License 2.0:

  app/connectors/whoop_api.py     from src/whoop.py (WhoopClient: the
                                  endpoints, scopes, authorization URL, token
                                  requests and paging)
  app/connectors/whoop.py         from src/models/cycle.py, recovery.py,
                                  sleep.py and workout.py (from_json: the field
                                  mapping, the score_state handling)
  app/connectors/whoop_export.py  from src/whoop_export.py and
                                  src/models/export.py (the export's files,
                                  columns, converters and checks)
  tests/fakes.py, WHOOP section   the export's CSV headers, from
                                  tests/conftest.py

Whoops ships no NOTICE file, and the copyright line of its licence's appendix
is the template's, unfilled: the copyright of that code stays with its
authors. The rest of Tributary is MIT.

